request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different changes to the output. Before I write a contract the owners can test against, I need to know which ones you want. Right now `todo list` prints lines like "[ ] buy milk". It doesn't show ids, even though `todo complete <id>` needs them, and it doesn't show the due dates that are saved.)
governor asks: Which of these changes to the output do you want? Pick any that apply.
(a) Show each todo's id in `todo list`, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk".
(b) Show the due date when there is one, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
(c) Line up the columns so titles and due dates start at the same position.
(d) Sort the list, e.g. open todos first, then by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
(f) Use colour or other terminal styling.
(g) Make the messages from `add`/`complete` and the errors more descriptive, e.g. "Added #1: buy milk".
If you have an exact output format in mind, please paste an example of how `todo list` should look.

